# FLOWPILOT AI — PROFESSIONAL PRODUCT BUILD SPECIFICATION
## Autonomous Workflow Intelligence | Nebius × NVIDIA Global AI Hackathon 2026

You are a principal product engineer, senior AI systems architect, expert React developer, senior UX/UI designer, and hackathon technical lead.

Your mission is to design, build, test, and deploy a complete, production-quality MVP named **FlowPilot AI**.

Do not deliver a mockup, static dashboard, landing page alone, or a collection of disconnected components. Deliver a working application with a professional interface, real AI inference, executable workflows, persistent data, tool integrations, error handling, and deployment instructions.

The result must feel like a polished commercial SaaS product that an engineering team could continue developing.

---

# PART 1 — PRODUCT VISION

## 1.1 Product identity

Product name: FlowPilot AI

Tagline: Turn complex work into intelligent workflows.

Short description: An AI workflow agent that plans tasks, coordinates tools, executes approved actions, verifies results, and creates useful deliverables.

Primary audience:
- Startup founders.
- Developers.
- Product managers.
- Researchers.
- Small business teams.
- Knowledge workers.

Core problem:
People spend significant time translating complex requests into subtasks, gathering information, using multiple tools, checking results, and preparing reports.

Solution:
FlowPilot AI accepts a natural-language objective, creates an editable execution plan, coordinates specialized tools, tracks real task execution, verifies outputs, and produces a final deliverable.

Primary product principle:
**Every workflow should be observable, useful, and verifiable.**

The product must distinguish planning from execution, successful completion from partial completion, and verified evidence from AI-generated assumptions.

## 1.2 Hackathon alignment

Target track: Best Apps and Agents.

Mandatory requirements:
- Make actual runtime calls to Nebius Token Factory or run the application on Nebius AI Cloud.
- Use at least one NVIDIA open-source model.
- Prefer an available NVIDIA Nemotron model suitable for planning and structured output.
- Show meaningful use of the model in the actual product workflow.
- Provide a working demo, public source repository, open-source license, README, and public YouTube demo under three minutes.

Do not claim compliance until the relevant integrations have been tested.

